<http://model.geneontology.org/6b01078700000430> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                  owl:versionIRI <http://model.geneontology.org/6b01078700000430> ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/modelstate> "development"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-7487-1936"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-11-25"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "CERS2 glucosylceramide synthesis (Human)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "http://geneontology.org"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Automated change 2025-08-14: GO:0010706 replaced by GO:0001574"^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Curated with GO AI HUB. Human de novo synthesis of C22 (CERS2) ceramide at the ER (SPT, KDSR, CERS2, DEGS1), CERT-independent delivery to UGCG at the Golgi for glucosylceramide synthesis, and GlcCer translocation by ABCA3."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "ER-to-Golgi transport of ceramide for glucosylceramide synthesis is CERT-independent (PMID:14685229, PMID:18068681, PMID:27775668). A COPII-vesicle route has been proposed (PMID:41856286) and a non-vesicular route reported (PMID:9677340). No mammalian gene product with a defined molecular function has been shown to carry ceramide to UGCG, so no transport activity is modelled. The step is shown as DEGS1 'provides input for' UGCG, with ceramide (CHEBI:72966) located in the cytoplasmic side of the ER membrane as DEGS1 output and in the cytoplasmic side of the Golgi membrane as UGCG input."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Edited 2026-09-25 (claude4go with curator): ABCA3 activity unit only, per repair of the companion model gomodel:680ad14200005180 from full text of Budani 2021 PMID:34597626. MF GO:0140351 glycosylceramide flippase (exoplasmic-to-cytosolic) replaced by GO:0034202 glycolipid floppase activity (cytosolic-to-lumenal). ABCB10 part_of galactosylceramide biosynthetic process removed (DU-145 cells make essentially no GalCer and GlcCer is not a GalCer precursor); both transporters now part_of GO:0006688 glycosphingolipid biosynthetic process (IMP; each KD reduced both globo-series and GM3 de novo synthesis). CC broadened from cis-Golgi network membrane to GO:0000139 Golgi membrane. Transporter MF, input, output, location and CC evidence are IC (binding plus KD phenotype; no transport assay or localization in the paper). "^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Follow-up 2026-09-25: curator does not accept the floppase reading for Golgi GlcCer translocation (cytoplasmic to lumenal leaflet). GO defines flippase/floppase topologically (exoplasmic vs cytosolic leaflet; the Golgi lumenal leaflet is exoplasmic), the paper itself does not assay direction, and the curator chose the direction-neutral parent GO:0140326 ATPase-coupled intramembrane lipid carrier activity, which already carries EXP annotations for ABCA3 and ABCA12. GO:0034202 glycolipid floppase activity therefore replaced by GO:0140326 on the ABC transporter unit(s) in this model. A GO ticket on whether GO:0140351 should cover Golgi lumenal import, or an NTR for a GlcCer-specific term, remains an option."^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <gomodel:685de18700004836> ;
                                                  <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/in_taxon> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606> .

